Scripture, commentary and cross-references are not covered by the grant above.
Both published packages carry them, so the terms travel here as well.

  Matos Soares               public domain, Brazilian law article 45
  Douay-Rheims               public domain, first published 1582 and 1610
  Clementine Vulgate         public domain, promulgated 1592
  Haydock, English           public domain, printed 1811 to 1814
  Haydock, Portuguese        machine translation of a public domain text
  Douay cross-references     CC0
  OpenBible cross-references CC BY 4.0, attribution required

Cross-references courtesy of OpenBible.info.

That notice is a condition of CC BY 4.0 and it is not satisfied by this file
alone. It travels inside every published cross-reference artifact and inside
every API response drawing on them, because an attribution a consumer never
reads is not an attribution.

LIMITS.md carries the full audit, the legal basis per asset and what this
repository refuses to publish at all.
